  "cves": [
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-80216",
      "publishedDate": "2026-08-26T02:51:27.805Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-08-26T02:51:27.805Z",
      "description": "A cleartext transmission of sensitive information vulnerability in the NFC interface of multiple Milesight IoT device models running affected firmware versions allows an unauthenticated attacker with physical proximity to retrieve LoRaWAN ABP NwkSKey and AppSKey values and D2D keys via an NFC read operation. The exposed keys can be used to decrypt LoRaWAN traffic, forge uplink and downlink frames, submit falsified sensor data, issue supported device commands, and cause subsequent legitimate frames to be rejected.",
      "severity": 7.6,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：Milesight AM102/102L V2\n🔓 漏洞类型：CWE-319 (CWE-319)\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
      "references": [
        {
          "url": "https://www.milesight.com/legal/vulnerabilities-in-some-milesight-sensors",
          "type": "reference"
        }
      ],
